      "message": "What I meant was:\n\n\tif (current_device-\u003eusb_flags \u0026\n\t\t    USB_SPI_CUSTOM_SPI_DEVICE_FULL_DUPLEX_SUPPORTED) {\n\t    \tif (current_device-\u003eusb_flags \u0026 USB_SPI_CUSTOM_SPI_DEVICE) {\n\t\t\tpacket-\u003ersp_config.feature_bitmap |\u003d\n\t\t\t\tUSB_SPI_FEATURE_FULL_DUPLEX_SUPPORTED;\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t/* Currently invalid */\n\t\t\tcprintf(\"Error\\n\");\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\nIs it possible for the common driver to be updated to handle full-duplex? If so, (CUSTOM\u003d0, FULL_DUPLEX\u003d1) is only temporarily invalid. Can you please tell me if I\u0027m missing something? I admit I don\u0027t have the whole context.",
